--TEST--
A class or interface constant writes its type, as every other binding does (ADR 0007 § 1)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// PHP's untyped constant parses, and the type read off the folded value is a
// guess the declaration never made: an interface constant has no such value
// to read, and one whose value has no constant form has nothing to read at
// all. Both used to reach the lowerer and panic there.
interface Limits {
    public const LIMIT = 9;
}
class Bounded implements Limits {
}
echo Limits::LIMIT, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0246]: a constant declares its type
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
